# local env files
.env*.local
.env*.bak
.env
# T-98 (PRE-L11 hardening) — THE OPERATOR BACKUPS WERE NOT IGNORED, AND THEY ARE BYTE COPIES OF
# .env.local. `.env*.bak` above only matches a name ENDING in `.bak`, so `.env.local.bak` was ignored
# while every name the window operators actually write — `.env.local.bak-refund-gate-<stamp>`,
# `.bak-modeb-gate-…`, `.bak-claims-gate-…`, `.bak-phase2-…` — was NOT (measured with
# `git check-ignore`). Those files carry DATABASE_URL, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, NEXTAUTH_SECRET, SMTP_PASS
# and INTERNAL_CRON_TOKEN verbatim, and the house session ritual is `git add .`. One `git add .` on a
# host that had run a window would have pushed every staging secret to GitHub. Anchored on the prefix,
# not on the suffix, so a new operator inventing a new stamp is covered before it is written.
.env*.bak*
.env.local.bak*

